  "observations": [
    "The development payload contains two tasks in each of the eight required semantic families and each task carries a repository-owned fixture path plus an existing test name.",
    "The invariant contract requires result shape, minimum multiplicity, ordering, NULL policy, failure policy and bounded clarification policy; compile-only and empty outcomes are rejected before semantic judging.",
    "The split identity includes seed group, semantic family and provider fixture identity, so superficial query spelling does not create a new partition group.",
    "The private judge is constructed as a separate judge-only object and forbidden answer keys are rejected from repair payloads; no judge answers are stored in the development corpus.",
    "Eight held-out groups are reserved but not materialized; materialization requires compared build identities and a frozen repair-prompt SHA-256, and the test suite verifies that answers are not exposed before that freeze."
  ],
